        "original_id": "3dce3eed-aea9-5cd7-af28-affc91eaa61f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arnold Burns, Edwin Meese, Ronald Reagan, Weld\n- Roles: Attorney General of the United States, attorney, law professor, author\n- Organizations: Republican Party, Reagan Presidential Transition Team, Reagan White House, Congress\n- Events: Meese's resignation, congressional appearance\n\nFacts:\n- Edwin Meese III was born on December 2, 1931.\n- Edwin Meese III is an American attorney, law professor, author, and member of the Republican Party.\n- Edwin Meese III served in Ronald Reagan's gubernatorial administration from 1967 to 1974.\n- Edwin Meese III served on the Reagan Presidential Transition Team in 1980.\n- Edwin Meese III served in the Reagan White House from 1981 to 1985.\n- Edwin Meese III became the 75th Attorney General of the United States and served from 1985 to 1988.\n- In July 1988, Arnold Burns and Weld appeared before Congress.\n- Edwin Meese resigned from office later in July 1988, shortly after Arnold Burns and Weld appeared before Congress.",
